    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a matchup against Will Warren, with the park factor and platoon advantage inflating his score well into the elite tier. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable matchup against Stock, further bolstered by wind conditions that boost his power potential, despite a minor penalty for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), **Kyle Tucker** (73.93), and **Andy Pages** (72.19) round out our most potent starts; both **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Andy Pages** are the primary beneficiaries of playing in high-favorable ballparks against pitchers with high expected ERAs, allowing us to leverage their current recency form for maximum Roto utility.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Wade Meckler** (51.24) on the bench. While his leadoff spot and platoon advantage provided a solid foundation, the optimizer ultimately favored the higher-upside profiles of **Sam Antonacci** and **Drake Baldwin** to round out the back end of the lineup. The primary risk to today\u2019s projections remains the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key pieces, including **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Coby Mayo**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Wade Meckler**. We are monitoring the official lineups closely, as any deviation in the assumed batting order\u2014particularly for **Nasim Nunez**\u2014could dampen the aggressive projections currently driving our efficiency scores. Additionally, while **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) ranks highly, managers should be aware that he faces a pitcher in Chris Bassitt who effectively suppresses stolen bases, which may slightly cap his total fantasy point contribution despite the favorable park factors.",
